      "source": [
        "# 🧵 Strings in Python\n",
        "\n",
        "A **string** is just a *sequence of characters* (in Python, Unicode characters). Picture a train 🚂 — each coach is one character, and every coach has a seat number called an **index**.\n",
        "\n",
        "**What this notebook covers**\n",
        "- Creating strings\n",
        "- Accessing characters (indexing & slicing)\n",
        "- Why strings can't be changed (immutability)\n",
        "- Common built-in functions\n",
        "- Useful string methods\n",
        "- Operations on strings\n",
        "\n",
        "> ▶️ Run each cell (**Shift + Enter**) and read the comment above it. Every \"error\" shown here is **intentional** — it teaches a rule."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "8YcoDm36BRir"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 1. Creating Strings\n",
        "\n",
        "Single, double, or triple quotes all create a string — pick whichever is convenient."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 4,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "0EvUlMdEBRir",
        "outputId": "6042df83-e7b1-45d1-da3a-4a7e62edc98e"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "hello hello hello hello hello\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# All of these create the same string \"hello\"\n",
        "s1 = 'hello'          # single quotes\n",
        "s2 = \"hello\"          # double quotes\n",
        "s3 = '''hello'''      # triple quotes (also allows multi-line)\n",
        "s4 = \"\"\"hello\"\"\"      # triple double quotes\n",
        "s5 = str('hello')     # using the str() constructor\n",
        "\n",
        "print(s1, s2, s3, s4, s5)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "60nFByRmBRit"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Convert other types into a string** with `str()`:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 5,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "N2_1T4I6BRit",
        "outputId": "3cdbc3c3-4647-46f0-f971-5b5bbad61393"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "34 -> <class 'str'>\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "n = 34          # this is an integer\n",
        "n = str(n)      # now it is the string \"34\"\n",
        "print(n, \"->\", type(n))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "fX8M7u5HBRit"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Quotes inside a string\n",
        "\n",
        "- Use **double quotes** outside when the text contains an apostrophe.\n",
        "- A single-quote string breaks if the text also has a single quote."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 6,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "dVGEK1-kBRit",
        "outputId": "8417227c-fcde-460e-ee66-148d901a2b23"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "it's my bike\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "text = \"it's my bike\"   # ✅ works: outer \" , inner '\n",
        "print(text)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 8,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "gYe2SLqABRiu",
        "outputId": "acd7ecd2-cde2-4219-ec4e-4ae766b539b2"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "it's my bike\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# ❌ This breaks -> text = 'it's my bike'\n",
        "#    Python thinks the string ends at the apostrophe:\n",
        "#    SyntaxError: unterminated string literal\n",
        "# ✅ Fix: use double quotes, OR escape the apostrophe with a backslash \\'\n",
        "text = 'it\\'s my bike'\n",
        "print(text)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "gjN5aIiMBRiu"
      },
      "source": [
        "Triple quotes let a string span **multiple lines**:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Fj058VLKBRiu",
